MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_001: This detestable sun... Were it not for my mission, this\nland would have no hold over me.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_002: You detest the sun? Perhaps you should not have\ntaken up missionary work.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_003: Ah, Dietrich! You are quite correct.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_004: And you do well to recall my vocation.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_005: You honor me by taking an interest in it.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_006: That the Church of Seiros would extend its reach to\nDagda surprises me. It seems notable.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_007: It has been over 260 years since Garreg Mach, our\nbase of operations, was founded.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_008: And since then, the church has become the\ndominant faith in Fódlan.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_009: Yet, there are many places the faith has yet to reach.\nPlaces that do not submit to Adrestian rule.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_010: In an effort to spread the good word, the church has\ndispatched missionaries far and wide.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_011: And so you were sent to Dagda.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_012: I have come to realize, however, that there is a thing\nmore troublesome than the sun's rays found here.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_013: I would hear of it.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_014: The sway the temples hold over the land's people.\nDagdan faith is incompatible with Fódlan's.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_015: With the gods themselves present in the flesh, how\ncan the Church of Seiros hope to compete? 
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_016: My current plan is to continue gathering information\nand record my findings for the archbishop.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_017: Hrmmm...
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_018: Disinterested, are you? Yet it was you who asked. It\nseems you struggle to make conversation.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_019: I had some curiosity. Nothing more.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_020: {SetColor=Gray}We cannot meet as equals in the conversational\narena, then? These beasts...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_021: Something on your mind, I see.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_022: Not as such. I have resolved to select a topic that you\nmay find more engaging when next we meet.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_023: That is fine. I trust your wisdom.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_C_024: It pleases me to hear it.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_001: Ahhh...
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_002: You have been gazing at the moon for some time.\nI can see you are quite taken with it.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_003: It is truly beautiful, isn't it?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_004: Radiant. Captivating. The moon in Fódlan and the\nmoon in Dagda are both unceasingly beautiful.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_005: You truly appreciate beauty, don't you, Dietrich?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_006: Life is transient, painted in blood, and death is ever\npresent. Beauty stirs the soul.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_007: Yet why I am so drawn to it... I could not say.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_008: In the distant past, people feared the moon. They\nheld that it drove people mad.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_009: The diviners of old are said to have considered it\na symbol of illusion. Deception.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_010: I heard you use a different name. Is Fabio\na deception?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_011: Anacharsis, you mean. Yes, the name Fabio is false.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_012: It is not a pseudonym—not precisely. It is the name\nthis body originally bore.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_013: Hm? Explain yourself.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_014: This body is merely a vessel. I have borrowed both\nthis form and its name from another.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_015: I have no particular attachment to them. On a\npractical level, they serve my aims.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_016: In fact, Dietrich... Were you to desire it...
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_017: I could adopt the form of a woman so beautiful I\nwould shine like the moon, even at your side.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_018: Of course, I would need to seek out such a beauty...\nand borrow her form.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_019: There is no need. You are fine as you are.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_020: I may well have begun to take a liking to you.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_021: You... You have? Well. If that is how you feel, then I\nshall be pleased to retain this form.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_022: What is it that stirs within me?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_023: Tell me, though... Why? Would you see beauty\nattained this way a deception?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_024: Beautiful, ugly... The surface is not all there is of\nbeauty, you know.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_025: The things I esteem are strength and purity.\nNothing else.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_026: What form they take is irrelevant. Man or woman...it\nis the same to me.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_027: The way you are living—that is where your beauty\nlies, Fabio.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_028: Ahh! I am honored to hear you say so.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_029: Hm... Anacharsis, wasn't it? That sounds so formal.\nI will continue to call you Fabio.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_B_030: Of course, Dietrich. All things will be as you wish\nthem to be.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_001: Today I found a worthy opponent to be my prey.\nA fine battle, it was.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_002: Dietrich... May I examine Answerer?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_003: Very well.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_004: Fascinating. You seem to be capable of drawing such\npower from it as to exceed its design...
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_005: It is as if Answerer is resonating with your strength\nand beauty.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_006: How is it that you can divine this?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_007: Before, I told you that it was we Agarthans who\ncrafted the Heroes' Relics.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_008: It is I who created Answerer, Dietrich.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_009: You...forged this blade?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_010: Heroes' Relics, as they are now called, draw the\npower from Crest Stones—the hearts of dragons.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_011: Simply stated, the stone is set in a housing of bone to\nchannel its terrible destructive power.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_012: And if you examine a relic, you can see how its\ncreator's personality is expressed in its design.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_013: Take the thermal dissipation system for Answerer's\nCrest Stone, for example. Have you considered it?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_014: I had not... Do you wish it back?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_015: Hardly. In fact, I am moved by your ability to exceed\nmy expectations for the blade.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_016: Truth told, you continue to exceed my expectations\non all fronts. I doubt I will ever tire of observing you.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_017: You should know I was the one who gave Lamine\nboth Answerer and the Rafail Gem so long ago.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_018: She wielded both magic and blade with such skill\nand beauty. I found myself rapt.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_019: So I sampled her tissue, cultivated it, and created\nbeings that I hoped would match her...
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_020: I experimented with these subjects for many moons.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_021: All that time, and that work came to naught. None\nI created could hope to match Lamine.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_022: When we met, you noted our resemblance\nimmediately... Was that why?
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_023: Yes. I find myself drawn even more strongly to you\nthan I was to her.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_024: {SetColor=Gray}I have come to understand your feelings, Periandros...\nLaugh at me if you wish.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_025: If you so will it, Dietrich, I would follow you\nwherever you may go.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_026: Yet we are of different make, are we not? I will meet\nmy end much sooner than you will.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_027: I would not mind it, Dietrich. Not if I were present\nfor your final moments.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_028: Hmhm. Your beauty is pure. Let us go onward, then.\nTogether.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_029: I swear that when that day does come, I will burn\nthe moment of your death upon my heart.
MID_SE_Dit_Fab_A_030: Yes... I am sure that none other will meet an end so\nmighty and beautiful as yours.